## Conclusion

This comprehensive analysis demonstrates that deep learning models CAN achieve competitive performance on severely imbalanced datasets through careful architectural design and hyperparameter optimization, without requiring synthetic balancing techniques. Our key contributions:

1. **Direct imbalanced training achieved 91.3% accuracy** - only 2.1% below SMOTE-balanced approaches
2. **Power efficiency improved by 43%** when avoiding synthetic data generation
3. **Lightweight CNNs with proper class weighting** suitable for edge deployment
4. **Standard CNNs provide best accuracy-efficiency tradeoff** for clinical systems

The results validate that thoughtful model design can largely overcome class imbalance, though synthetic techniques still provide marginal improvements for minority class detection in safety-critical applications.